## Model & Ollama (verified 2026-10-17)

- **Base model tag:** `gemma4:e4b` (4B effective, ~3–5 GB Q4, needs 6–8 GB RAM)
- **Custom model name:** `zerotrace-analyst` (created via `agent/ollama/Modelfile`)
- **Ollama endpoint for inference:** `POST http://localhost:11434/api/chat`
- **Structured output:** Pass the full JSON Schema object as `format` field — NOT `"json"` string
- **Response location:** `response.message.content` (a JSON string — must be parsed)
- **Stream:** Always `stream: false` for ZeroTrace
- **Temperature:** `0.1` (fixed for deterministic scoring)
- **Context window:** `num_ctx 8192` (sufficient for our ~1200-token prompt)
- **Keep-alive:** `10m` (sent per-request in the request body, NOT in Modelfile)
- **OpenAI-compat endpoint** (`/v1/chat/completions`) does NOT support the `format` schema — always use `/api/chat`
- **Gemma 4 does NOT emit `<think>` blocks** — response is direct JSON when format is set

### Open Assumptions (confirm when Ollama is installed)
- A1: `gemma4:e4b` tag exists on this machine after `ollama pull`
- A2: Model emits clean JSON at temperature 0.1 (verify with `smoke-test.sh`)
- A3: `PARAMETER num_ctx 8192` in Modelfile is honored (`ollama show zerotrace-analyst`)
- A4: Response time < 30 s on demo hardware
- A5: `keep_alive` in Modelfile PARAMETER syntax may not be supported — set per-request instead
- A6: JSON Schema subset accepted without errors (confirm via smoke test)

