## Architecture Decisions Log

### 2026-10-17 — Initial build (Phase 0: docs + model assets)
- Chose `gemma4:e4b` over `gemma4:12b` for RAM efficiency (6–8 GB vs 12–16 GB)
- Structured output via `/api/chat` `format` field — confirmed working by Ollama docs
- Fallback engine (`LLM_MODE=demo`) ensures demo never fails if Ollama is unavailable
- `recommendedKillPid` override added as a server-side trust boundary
- All 14 validation checks passed (`node agent/scripts/validate-examples.js`)
- 20 files committed and pushed to `main` (commit b01d5a9)

### 2026-10-17 — Phase 1: Full Backend & Bauhaus Frontend Implementation
- **Backend (Express :5001)**: All routes implemented (`/api/stream` SSE, `/api/simulate-attack`, `/api/contain`, `/api/health`). Zero real OS commands, in-memory store, 13-point validator. Verified against AC-1 to AC-7.
- **Frontend (Next.js 15 App Router)**: Implemented full dashboard in the **Bauhaus Constructivist design system**:
  - Primary colors: Red `#D02020`, Blue `#1040C0`, Yellow `#F0C020`, Black `#121212`, Canvas `#F0F0F0`.
  - Typography: Google Font 'Outfit' (900 black, uppercase, tight tracking) + 'JetBrains Mono' for commands/PIDs.
  - Binary radii (`rounded-none` and `rounded-full`), hard offset shadows (`4px/8px`), tactile active press animation.
  - Components: `GeometricLogo`, `StatusBanner`, `ScenarioControls`, `IncidentCard`, `ReasoningTrail`, `MitreBadges`, `ContainmentButton`, `PostmortemExport`, `IncidentFeed`.
- Verified production build (`npm run build` static prerendering succeeded).

